    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** serving as the cornerstone of our offensive strategy. Boasting an elite score of 81.92, **Caminero** draws a high-leverage matchup against Bieber. Despite the veteran pitcher's pedigree, the advanced metrics favor **Caminero** heavily, bolstered by his prime spot in the three-hole and an xwOBA of 0.379. Alongside him, **Colt Keith** represents our next strongest play (68.51) against Dobnak. The combination of Dobnak\u2019s inflated 5.65 xERA and **Colt Keith**\u2019s favorable platoon split and #3 order placement provides the ideal environment for a multi-hit performance that bolsters our team AVG and run production.\n\nWhile **Lars Nootbaar** (57.79) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (55.91) fall into the marginal start category, they remain essential for today's volume. **Lars Nootbaar** benefits from a dynamic platoon edge against Pfaadt that helps mitigate park factors, while **Kazuma Okamoto** is locked in as a steady contributor despite a neutral R/R matchup. **Dillon Dingler** sits on the edge of the marginal threshold at 51.71; while his raw base projection is modest, the porous 5.65 xERA of Dobnak provides a statistical safety net that warrants his inclusion. Unfortunately, our elite core\u2014including **Yordan Alvarez**, **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Kyle Schwarber**\u2014are sidelined by a scheduling off-day, severely limiting our access to high-upside stolen base threats like **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Trea Turner**, which forces us to play a more station-to-station game tonight. \n\nManaging the depth chart remains a focus for the Zebras, as players like **Christian Yelich**, **Caleb Durbin**, and **Hyeseong Kim** remain available should any late-inning weather alerts impact the status of our current starters. We are closely monitoring the lineup stability of **Carson Benge** and **Gary Sanchez** relative to the bench depth of **Nelson Velazquez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**. While none of our bench options eclipsed the starters tonight, **Nelson Velazquez** came closest to cracking the lineup due to his power upside, but was ultimately held out as we prioritize the higher floor provided by our current infield configuration. No significant weather risks are reported, allowing us to proceed with the posted rotation as scheduled.",
